{"version":"1","id":"dc","handle":"dc","name":"DataCamp","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/dc","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-0.5668,"y":-1.5954,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2022-04-25T06:47:27.527Z","oldest_post_at":"2019-03-18T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.003333,"listicle_ratio":0.02,"question_ratio":0.02,"avg_read_time":9.24,"summary_length_avg":348.44,"title_length_avg":39.486667,"title_length_var":354.109822,"tag_entropy":2.907142,"tag_diversity":0.096667,"top_tag_share":0.043333,"avg_upvotes":0.066667,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.006667,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.142857,"zero_engagement_share":0.96,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.868727,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.090909},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.4412,-6.1765],"cadence_depth":[5.1029,5.7059],"hype_variety":[-2.4706,-3.1029],"title_style":[0.8382,5.2353]},"top_tags":[["data-science",15],["machine-learning",6],["python",4],["career",3],["general-programming",3],["big-data",2],["deep-learning",2],["science",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["How to Become a SQL Expert","Data Visualization with Bokeh Tutorial: Getting Started","Machine Learning, Pipelines, Deployment and MLOps Tutorial"],"outlier":["Building a Scalable Data Strategy with IPTOP: Infrastructure, People, Tools, Organization, and Processes"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"MgJc4UgJ4","title":"How to Become a Data Scientist","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/blog-how-to-become-a-data-scientist","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-become-a-data-scientist-mgjc4ugj4","summary":"The path to becoming a data scientist is long. You need to master a wide set of skills such as coding, math, and communication. Here, we show you an effective and attractive way to learn what you need to get started in the data science world. The checklist is for beginners, yet if you are not quite a beginner you may still gain some useful insights.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:47:27.527Z"},{"id":"Ncb0RlBNS","title":"Data Analyst Skills for Career Success","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/blog-data-analyst-skills-for-career-success","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/data-analyst-skills-for-career-success-ncb0rlbns","summary":"Data analysis can offer you job security, the potential for remote work, high pay, and interesting challenges. While analysts have existed in organizations for years, new tech tools and a major influx in data collection in organizations is reigniting serious interest in this career path. While graduate programs and certificates are rapidly appearing, professionals still have the chance to make their way into this field.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/795dbd783390d5bd686770d15d1d1f1d","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:46:30.979Z"},{"id":"oZLA1jCpU","title":"How Data & Culture Unlock Digital Transformation","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/how-data-culture-unlock-digital-transformation","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-data-culture-unlock-digital-transformation-ozla1jcpu","summary":"Mai AlOwaish is Chief Data Officer at Gulf Bank. She outlines how a people and data-first approach can unlock the value of digital transformation. In her current position, Mai leads the data analytics practice in Gulf Bank and oversees the data strategy and implementation of data science and analytics use cases.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:45:05.553Z"},{"id":"ntXWh51y9","title":"Ten Lessons for Future Data Scientists","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/ten-lessons-for-future-data-scientists","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ten-lessons-for-future-data-scientists-ntxwh51y9","summary":"More and more people are breaking into data science every day. The Harvard Business Review declared data scientist the sexiest job of the 21st century. DataCamp has a large catalog of courses where you can learn both Python and R. In the beginning, it will hurt. But be patient. You are not alone.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:42:28.232Z"},{"id":"1rVtV0GMY","title":"Seven Tricks for Better Data Storytelling: Part II","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/seven-tricks-for-better-data-storytelling-2","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/seven-tricks-for-better-data-storytelling-part-ii-1rvtv0gmy","summary":"Data visualizations stand to benefit from adopting the age-old narrative structure. An audience is 22 times more likely to remember a fact when told a story. A data story starts with a background on the current situation, builds up to the central insight, and ends with a call to action.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:42:17.747Z"},{"id":"IUbndx-ux","title":"What is Data Engineering?","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/what-is-data-engineering","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-data-engineering--iubndx-ux","summary":"As of 2021 there are 23.8 billion devices connected to the internet. 58% of those are IoT devices (smart home devices, connected self-driving cars, industrial devices) and the remaining 42% are non-IoT devices (laptops, smartphones, etc.) This means that nowadays data can come from various sources. All the different structured data that the world produces needs to be delivered to other components.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:38:54.203Z"},{"id":"LJ2G6qTyp","title":"Seven Tricks for Better Data Storytelling: Part I","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/blog/seven-tricks-for-better-data-storytelling-1","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/seven-tricks-for-better-data-storytelling-part-i-lj2g6qtyp","summary":"Subtle differences in design can profoundly impact the audience\u2019s interpretation of a data visualization. When delivering a supposedly objective data story, data storytellers should pay attention to details in charts that might amplify biases. The Gutenberg principle tells us that the most important information should be on the top left.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7aed07d5d040122e40c86c5701e0a322","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-25T06:37:26.414Z"},{"id":"hmreelKw9","title":"Normal Equation for Linear Regression Tutorial","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/tutorials/tutorial-normal-equation-for-linear-regression","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/normal-equation-for-linear-regression-tutorial-hmreelkw9","summary":"The Normal Equation is a closed-form solution used to find the value of  that minimizes the cost function. Gradient descent takes an analytical approach which means our parameters are updated gradually until convergence. The most obvious way in which the normal equation differs from gradient descent is that it\u2019s not taking steps directly to get the results.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4f85a487b7ff4377bd1726c05b5320f1","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-06T09:53:32.895Z"},{"id":"RMRLlMrRM","title":"How to Execute SQL Queries in Python and R Tutorial","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/tutorials/tutorial-how-to-execute-sql-queries-in-r-and-python","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-execute-sql-queries-in-python-and-r-tutorial-rmrllmrrm","summary":"Learn how to connect databases, populate databases, and run queries using Python and R. In this tutorial, we will learn how to load the COVID-19's impact on airport traffic dataset into our SQLite database. We will also learn to create tables from scratch using Pandas.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4f85a487b7ff4377bd1726c05b5320f1","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-04-04T13:08:46.118Z"},{"id":"D_TPDn6dm","title":"Data Visualization with Bokeh Tutorial: Plotting Data Structures","url":"https://www.datacamp.com/community/tutorials/tutorial-data-visualization-with-bokeh","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/data-visualization-with-bokeh-tutorial-plotting-data-structures-d-tpdn6dm","summary":"In this tutorial, you will learn how to plot data with NumPy arrays, dataframes in Pandas, and ColumnDataSource using Bokeh. In this example, we use the open-source S&P 500 stock data available on Kaggle. We want to see the correlation between Google's prices and Apple's prices.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4f85a487b7ff4377bd1726c05b5320f1","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-03-30T16:36:49.624Z"}],"similar_handles":["bair","inter","lirantal","arcnotes","cdfoundation"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"bair","handle":"bair","name":"BAIR","is_squad":false,"x":-0.6967,"y":-1.5286,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":140,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/bair","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.396594,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.003571,"avg_read_time":7.814286,"tag_diversity":0.257143},"top_tags_preview":[["machine-learning",32],["ai",24],["deep-learning",18]],"view_coords":{"eng